The current implementation returns a standard QuerySet which fetches all columns. By changing it to only select the primary key (`pk`), we avoid fetching unnecessary data (including the problematic `line` field) and improve performance. Since the collector only needs the objects to identify them for deletion (and doesn't access their attributes), selecting only the PK is sufficient.

